<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muluki Ain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1854</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Muluki Ain of 1854</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Muluki Ain is the national legal code of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> issued in 1854 under the Rana prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jang-bahadur-rana">Jang Bahadur Rana</a>. It codified civil and criminal law and placed every group in the kingdom within a single <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> hierarchy, from the 'sacred-thread-wearing' high castes through the 'liquor-drinking' castes down to the untouchables, with punishments varying by caste. It remained in force, much amended, until a new code replaced it in 1963.</p></div>
